Within that way of working, Claude was used for the following:
\begin{itemize}
\item to discuss how a method described in the literature could be implemented on this dataset, and to break a planned analysis into steps;
\item to draft parts of the analysis code, which the author then read, ran and revised;
\item to draft and revise passages of text, which the author then edited for content, accuracy and register;
\item to find and correct faults in code and in text, including checking reported numbers against the stored results;
\item to search for and summarise literature, which the author then read in the original before citing it.
\end{itemize}

