\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Mismatched data speeds.} Eye tracking is recorded at 120\,Hz, \ac{EDA} at 4\,Hz.
\item \textbf{Movement noise} in the wrist-worn \ac{EDA} and heart-rate sensors.
\item \textbf{Intermittent speech.} Visitors are silent for much of the visit, so any fusion model must accommodate empty segments.
\end{itemize}

\begin{sloppypar}
\begin{description}
\item[RQ1: Sensor Contribution and Representation.] How accurately are valence and arousal predicted for an unseen visitor from each of the five sensor streams alone and from their combinations, in mean \ac{CCC} over leave-one-participant-out folds, and how far do the preprocessing, alignment, and feature-representation choices searched here change that figure?

\item[RQ5: Personalisation.] Can visitor-specific calibration, including a labelled warm-up of 30 to 180 seconds taken from the held-out visitor's own session, raise \ac{CCC}, pooled \ac{QWK} and balanced accuracy for that visitor, and does the gain grow with the amount of calibration data?
\end{description}
\end{sloppypar}

