\insightsbox{Findings}{%
\begin{itemize}
\item Personalisation is not established at this cohort size. The pooled figures move in the expected direction in 21 of the 24 cells, yet none of the 48 paired tests survives correction.
\item The labelled warm-up responds to the amount of annotation it is given. Three minutes of the visitor's own ratings raises pooled agreement by up to $+0.3019$, on retro arousal, and on three of the four slices each shorter warm-up raises it less.
\item That lever is the one a museum cannot ask for. The only lever requiring no ratings lowers the continuous score on three of the four slices, by up to $0.0393$, while raising the ordinal one.
\end{itemize}}
